  "rule": "Background 7, vertical 4 line at the middle column cx, three 8 markers on the middle row cy (both edges and the line crossing). A multicoloured shape sits against the left of the line. The output keeps the input and paints every shape cell (y,x) at (2cy-y, 2cx-x): a 180-degree point reflection about the centre 8, onto the empty right side.",
  "scope": "Random mode samples odd grid sizes 9..29 wide and 7..29 tall. Default samples are about 60% square and 40% strictly non-square. The task fixtures are square 15..19, so other sizes and non-square grids are synthetic extensions. The line and marker are always placed in the middle column and row, so reflections never clip. Random shapes vary in: tapered depth profile with jitter, vertical extent (about 80% off-centre relative to the marker row), layer or band colouring with 2..6 colours, border thickness, an optional spine column, 0-2 holes, and an optional fringed end row. Explicit mode (size/width/height + top + rows) reconstructs the fixtures. Not supported: off-centre line or marker placement (which would require clipping), lines of other colours, shapes not touching the line, or shapes extending to the right side of the line.",
  "constraints": [
    "1132 fresh input-only point-rotation checks, including every supported random height/width combination; all original fixtures exact",
    "Every example distinguishes 180-degree rotation from plain horizontal reflection",
    "27 successful parameter controls; eight rejected controls after host adjudication of two critic expectations (unsupported width five and disconnected marker-touching shape)"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Line and marker are always central, so off-centre configurations with clipped reflections are not generated.",
    "Random shapes are always row-contiguous tapered profiles. They are structurally diverse but share a family style with the fixtures.",
    "The background, line and marker colours are fixed at 7, 4 and 8.",
    "The _sample_shape fallback after 60 attempts recolours the spine column with random colours. It is correct but visually less structured, and is expected to be rare.",
    "Relies on common.grid(width, height, color) returning height rows of width cells, as documented.",
    "Sampled agreement and shape controls do not prove complete coverage of all valid scenes."
  ],
